### How to use the `StringUtil` class

The `StringUtil` class provides two static methods for encoding strings: `encode()` and `removeEncodingFromPath()`. Here's an example of how you could use these methods:

```java
import java.io.File;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws UnsupportedEncodingException {
        String str = "Hello World";
        System.out.println("Encoded string: " + StringUtil.encode(str));
        
        File file = new File("test.txt");
        if (file.exists()) {
            System.out.println("Path with encoding: " + new String(file.getName().getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8), StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        } else {
            System.out.println("No path with encoding found.");
        }
    }
}
```

